---
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Accessibility statement — BluHeron Interactive"
  description="How this website practices what our studio preaches: WCAG 2.2 AA, reduced-motion design, keyboard navigation, and a real way to tell us when something's wrong."
>
  <article class="wrap page">
    <p class="kicker">Accessibility</p>
    <h1 class="display">Everyone means <em class="clay">everyone</em>.</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Accessibility isn't a checklist we run at the end — it's the reason this studio
        exists. Our platform, beacbeac, was co-designed with Blind, Low Vision, Deaf,
        Deafblind, and disabled community members. This website is held to the same standard.
      </p>

      <h2>What this site does</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Targets <strong>WCAG 2.2 Level AA</strong>, and aims higher where we can.
        </li>
        <li>
          Works completely without JavaScript — every page, every piece of content.
        </li>
        <li>
          Treats motion as an invitation, not a default: animation only runs if your system
          allows it (<code>prefers-reduced-motion</code>), and the homepage's moving artwork
          has a visible pause button that remembers your choice. The still version isn't a
          fallback — it's designed. Everything that moves can be paused — and nothing moves at
          all if your system asks for reduced motion.
        </li>
        <li>Is fully keyboard-navigable, with visible focus indicators and a skip link.</li>
        <li>Meets or exceeds 4.5:1 colour contrast for text, in both light and dark themes.</li>
        <li>Describes every meaningful image with alt text.</li>
        <li>Uses semantic HTML landmarks, built and checked for screen-reader navigation.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Something not working for you?</h2>
      <p>
        Tell us — genuinely. If any part of this site is hard to use with your assistive
        technology, browser, or connection, email
        <a href="mailto:alex@bluheroninteractive.com">alex@bluheroninteractive.com</a> and we
        will fix it. Feedback like this makes our work better everywhere, not just here.
      </p>

      <h2>Beyond this website</h2>
      <p>
        In our physical installations we design for many bodies and ways of experiencing:
        cooperative interfaces, multiple modes of interaction, and community advisors involved
        from the start of every project. Read more about
        <a href={withBase('/values/')}>how we work</a> or
        <a href={withBase('/beacbeac/')}>what access-first technology looks like</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    padding-block: clamp(48px, 7vw, 80px) clamp(56px, 8vw, 96px);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 28px;
    max-width: 860px;
  }

  .page em.clay {
    color: var(--clay);
  }

  .prose {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 18px;
  }

  .prose p,
  .prose li {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .prose h2 {
    font-size: 1.7rem;
    margin-top: 18px;
  }

  .prose ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.2em;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  code {
    font-size: 0.9em;
    background: var(--paper-2);
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 6px;
  }
</style>
